---
// The ready-made example game: a real TCG Live game with the opponent's
// name replaced by "Rival", and the decklist that was played, each with a
// copy button.
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CopyBlock from '../../components/CopyBlock.astro';
import Prompt from '../../components/Prompt.astro';
import { example } from '../../lib/example';
---
<Docs
  title="Example game"
  description="A complete Pokémon TCG Live game and its decklist to copy, so you can try tcgreplay without a game of your own."
>
  <h1>Example game</h1>
  <p>
    No game of your own to hand? Use this one. It is a real game from Pokémon TCG Live: NicJackson playing Mega Lucario
    ex against a Mew ex, Bronzong and Mega Lopunny ex deck, a close loss, 4 prizes to 6. The opponent's player name has
    been replaced with <strong>Rival</strong>.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Copy the decklist and the battle log below.</li>
    <li>Paste both into a chat with your assistant, with a prompt like this one:</li>
  </ol>
  <Prompt text="Here's a game from TCG Live and my decklist. Import it and review it with me." />
  <p>
    The assistant imports the game, says whether the import was complete, and gives you a link to the board. See
    <a href="/docs/import">importing a game</a> for what to expect.
  </p>

  <h2>The decklist</h2>
  <CopyBlock text={example.deck} label="Example decklist" tall />

  <h2>The battle log</h2>
  <p>Every line of the game, from setup to the result.</p>
  <CopyBlock text={example.log} label="Example battle log" tall class="example-log" />
</Docs>
